---
title: Asset Management Library
---
# Asset Management Library

This is an opt-in local module exporting the six initial Asset Management structural
schemas defined by `docs/language-spec-v0.3.md` section 13. These types are shape
contracts only: they express no severity/likelihood scale, score formula, identifier
policy, required relationship, or other domain rule beyond their declared fields. They
are not core defaults and are only visible to a document that explicitly imports them,
for example:

```text
import { Asset, FailureMode } from "./libraries/asset-management.amx"
```

Domain review is required before these schemas are represented as stable Asset
Management standards.

```amx
export type FailureMode {
  id: String
  name: String
  description?: String? = null
  severity: Number
  occurrence: Number
  detectability?: Number? = null
}

export type Risk {
  id: String
  failureMode: FailureMode
  likelihood: Number
  consequence: Number
  score?: Number? = null
}

export type Strategy {
  id: String
  name: String
  description?: String? = null
  targetRiskIds: String[] = []
}

export type Asset {
  id: String
  name: String
  assetClass: String
  criticality: Number
  failureModes: FailureMode[] = []
}

export type MaintenanceTask {
  id: String
  assetId: String
  strategyId?: String? = null
  title: String
  intervalDays: Number
  estimatedCost?: Number? = null
}

export type LifecycleCost {
  assetId: String
  acquisitionCost: Number
  operatingCost: Number
  maintenanceCost: Number
  disposalCost?: Number? = null
}
```
